error[E0133]: <div innerHTML={p.Body}>: innerHTML takes a ui.RawHTML, and p.Body is a string
  --> err_innerhtml.vuka:11:14
   |
11 |     return <div innerHTML={p.Body} />
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: wrap it in ui.Sanitize(p.Body) when users write it, or ui.RawHTML(p.Body) when it is trusted

error[E0133]: <div innerHTML={"<b>bold</b>"}>: innerHTML takes a ui.RawHTML, and "<b>bold</b>" is a string
  --> err_innerhtml.vuka:15:14
   |
15 |     return <div innerHTML={"<b>bold</b>"} />
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: wrap it in ui.Sanitize("<b>bold</b>") when users write it, or ui.RawHTML("<b>bold</b>") when it is trusted

error[E0133]: <div innerHTML={ui.Text(p.Body)}>: innerHTML takes a ui.RawHTML, and ui.Text(p.Body) is a ui.Node
  --> err_innerhtml.vuka:19:14
   |
19 |     return <div innerHTML={ui.Text(p.Body)} />
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a ui.Node goes in as a child: <div>{ui.Text(p.Body)}</div>

For more information about this error, try `vuka explain E0133`.
